# Pipeline-generated deliverables/diagnostics (written by a run; not source). The
# latter also holds the command sandbox's ephemeral per-run scratch — a private
# CARGO_HOME/RUSTUP_HOME + linker TMPDIR under sandbox/ (docs/command-sandbox.md §3).
/certora/
/.certora_internal/

# Build outputs (cargo-build-sbf / crucible).
/target/
crashes/
# `Cargo.lock` is COMMITTED here, unlike the other scenarios. `cargo-build-sbf` runs the Solana
# platform-tools cargo (1.79), which cannot parse an `edition2024` manifest or honour a
# `rust-version` above its own — and a free resolution now picks several. The committed lock holds
# the transitive set below both boundaries; delete it and this scenario stops building.
# Fuzzing artifacts (crucible run: corpus + explore-mode ./corpus, ./output).
/corpus/
/output/

